<%# What stands where the gilded hall has columns: a rose climbing the edge of the room.
    Expects: side ("left" | "right").

    Same reasoning as this skin's cornice - "slice" rather than "none", because a vertically
    stretched flower is an ellipse. Here the viewBox is far TALLER than the element, so the WIDTH
    is what binds the scale: the vine always spans the column's full width at its natural
    proportions, and the surplus height is cropped off the bottom. The vine repeats every 200
    units, so where the crop falls is invisible.

    The right-hand copy is mirrored by CSS (transform: scaleX(-1) on the shared column class),
    which is why nothing here branches on `side` beyond the class name - two vines growing the
    same way up both edges would read as wallpaper rather than as a frame. %>
<svg class="throne-hall__column throne-hall__column--<%= side %>" viewBox="0 0 100 2400"
     preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMin slice" role="presentation">
  <% const SEG = 200; %>
  <% for (let i = 0; i < 12; i++) { const y = i * SEG; %>
    <%# The stem: two quadratics into an S, swinging between x=34 and x=66. A single cubic pulls
        far too weakly at this aspect ratio and comes out almost straight. %>
    <path d="M50 <%= y %> Q 18 <%= y + 50 %> 50 <%= y + 100 %> Q 82 <%= y + 150 %> 50 <%= y + 200 %>"
          fill="none" stroke="var(--throne-stone)" stroke-width="3.2" stroke-linecap="round" />
    <%# A thorn or two, so the stem reads as a rose cane and not as a cable. %>
    <path d="M40 <%= y + 26 %> l -4 -3 M60 <%= y + 126 %> l 4 -3"
          fill="none" stroke="var(--throne-stone)" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.8" />

    <use href="#rose-leaf-art" transform="translate(44 <%= y + 20 %>) rotate(-38) scale(1.25)" />
    <use href="#rose-leaf-art" transform="translate(56 <%= y + 74 %>) rotate(150) scale(-1.25 1.25)" />
    <use href="#rose-leaf-art" transform="translate(56 <%= y + 122 %>) rotate(34) scale(1.25)" />
    <use href="#rose-leaf-art" transform="translate(44 <%= y + 176 %>) rotate(-146) scale(-1.25 1.25)" />

    <%# Two blooms and a bud per repeat, set on alternating sides of the stem so the eye reads a
        climb rather than a stack. %>
    <use href="#rose-bud-art" transform="translate(64 <%= y + 32 %>) rotate(24) scale(1.15)" />
    <use href="#rose-bloom-art" transform="translate(30 <%= y + 56 %>) scale(1.55)" />
    <use href="#rose-bloom-art" transform="translate(70 <%= y + 152 %>) scale(1.35)" />
    <use href="#rose-bud-art" transform="translate(36 <%= y + 186 %>) rotate(-20) scale(1)" />
  <% } %>
</svg>
